# Extraction stub — QC-2401.11056

**Note:** nougat was NOT run for this paper. Method reading and equation transcription were done via `pdftotext work/paper.pdf work/paper.txt`, which was sufficient because:

1. The numerical claims in this replication (permutation invariance C1/C2, Eq. (8) closed form C3, X-vs-GM comparison C4) come from an **independent statevector reimplementation** built from the rank-1 operator form `U_GM(β) = I + (e^{-iβ}-1)|s><s|`, not from paper-extracted numbers.
2. The single equation transcribed from the paper — Eq. (8), `P(ρ, r) = sin²((2r+1) · arcsin(√ρ))` with threshold `ρ_Th(r) = sin²(π/(4r+2))` — is a well-known Grover-algorithm identity that we cross-checked against Grover's original derivation, not just against the PDF.

## Paper metadata
- arXiv: 2401.11056 (v3, 12 Aug 2024)
- Title: Analytical results for the Quantum Alternating Operator Ansatz with Grover Mixer
- Authors: Guilherme Adamatti Bridi (UFRJ), Franklin de Lima Marquezino (UFRJ / U. Latvia)
- Local PDF: work/paper.pdf
- Local text: work/paper.txt (pdftotext output)

## If a nougat/mmd extraction is later required
Run:
```
nougat work/paper.pdf --out extraction/ --model 0.1.0-base
```
This will produce `extraction/paper.mmd` with LaTeX-preserved equations. Not required for the numerical replication above.
